# Reference scans. Large, copyrighted, and not ours to redistribute.
# spec/sources.md records what each one is and where it came from.
docs/*.pdf

# OCaml / dune
_build/
# No trailing slash: "_opam/" matches only a directory, and a worktree that
# shares the one switch holds _opam as a *symlink* to it. That symlink was
# committed once (26c68b5) and, checked out in the main repo where its target
# is its own path, became a self-referential loop over the real switch.
_opam
*.install
*.merlin

# Node / VSCode extension
node_modules/
editor/vscode/out/
editor/vscode/*.vsix

# Working files
.DS_Store

# Python
__pycache__/
*.pyc

# Framebuffer PNGs: the CLI writes one beside any .bas that draws, so a
# conformance case leaves one behind whenever it is run by hand. The suite
# compares digests (.digest), never these; .actual.png is the frame the
# harness dumps on a digest mismatch.
test/conformance/*.png

# The extension's runtime dependencies are vendored deliberately (Alex's
# ruling, 2026-08-17): the extension installs by copying a directory and has
# no build step, and today proved that is the property that matters -- it was
# silently dead for weeks because the installed copy was stale, and an
# "npm install" step is the same class of hazard, skippable and quietly
# half-completable. 3.1MB in git is the cheaper failure.
# node_modules/.bin is NOT vendored: it holds only CLI shims, which nothing
# here launches, and they are symlinks. A tracked symlink is what destroyed
# the opam switch this morning, so the tree carries none.
!editor/vscode/node_modules/
editor/vscode/node_modules/.bin/
